4. Empty-owner window mechanism support (strace, no code change): Node
   `writeFileSync(path, data, { flag: 'wx' })` performs two system calls —
   `openat(..., O_CREAT|O_EXCL|...)` (creates the file EMPTY) followed later by
   `write(2)` of the payload. Between them the canonical `owner.json` exists but
   parses as empty => a stale reaper can judge a live acquirer's freshly mkdir'd
   directory as stale (readOwner returns ''), detach it with `renameSync`, and the
   preempted acquirer's fd write + rootDir-level diagnostic-mirror publish still
   succeed, so BOTH processes complete `acquireRootLock` as owners
   (lifecycle.ts L122-131: success = mkdir + owner write + mirror publish with no
   post-write re-verification that canonical still names this handle).

Rate profile (CI-shaped rounds, real workers, production code):
  idle machine:          0 doubles / ~500+ rounds (incl. 60 sequential vitest runs)
  loaded machine:        2 doubles / ~240 driver rounds (~0.8%)
  CI runner (observed):  1 failure / ~18 single-round canary executions
  => preemption-of-the-owner-in-the-create->write-gap is the trigger; probability
     scales with CPU contention (GitHub-hosted runners' noise suffices to fire).
